{
 "_comment": "WP-11.4, Ruling C part 2 (5 Sep 2026). THE UNSOURCED `measured` PARAMETERS AS THEY STOOD WHEN THE GATE WENT IN. `build/check_kits.py` refuses any `measured` parameter with no `source` on itself and no `sources[]` on its slot UNLESS its (node, slot, parameter) triple is in this list. Adding a new one is then refused BY IDENTITY, which the old net ratchet could not do -- sourcing one figure while adding another kept the total at 542 and the build green. REMOVING a triple from this list is a ONE-WAY DOOR: it means the parameter now carries a source, and it may never be added back. Part 1 of the ruling is NOT given: nothing here is re-kinded, and this is a record of a debt, not a licence. 5 Sep 2026: 542 -> 536. Six triples walked through the one-way door when WP-11.4 Ruling A gave them a `precedents/<id>#measurements[<n>]` source that check_precedents.py compares with the figure. The door only opens outward: a triple removed here may never be added back.",
